  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nWe propose a multi-resolution optimization strategy combined with simulated annealing to escape local optima. The central idea is to smooth the non-convex objective function using LogSumExp (LogSE) penalization and globally optimize by tensorizing the convolution operation. The symmetric structure of the step function suggests that we can decompose it into a few active symmetric patterns, which we optimize collectively. \n\nThis approach addresses the bottleneck of local optimization by:\n- Using a novel LogSE surrogate that:\n  * Flattens the objective landscape\n  * Allows gradient-based optimization\n  * Maintains the equivalence to the original problem as the smoothing parameter \u2192 \u221e\n- Incorporating multi-resolution analysis through piecewise interpolation to discover fine-grained structure while maintaining global properties\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nWe represent the indicator function h(x) as a vector h \u2208 [0,1]\u207f with \u2211h = n/2.\n\nObjective to minimize:\nC_5 = max\u2096 {\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx} \nwhere dx=2/n\n\nSmoothed Objective (F(h,\u03b1)):\nF(h,\u03b1) = ln(1/\u03b1) + max\u2096 [\u03b1\u00b7nork(h)(1-h)(k) - ln(sum\u2096 exp(\u03b1\u00b7nork(h)(1-h)(k)))\n\u2192 As \u03b1\u2192\u221e, F(h,\u03b1) \u2192 min\u2096 nork(h)(1-h)(k), the original objective\n\nTensorized Optimization:\nLet U be the transformation matrix computing pairwise overlaps:\nU_{ij,kl} = [1_{i\u2264j} - 1_{i>j}]_{ij} \u00b7 [1_{k\u2264l} - 1_{k>l}]_{kl}\nThen h\u0303 = Uh represents all shifted values \nThe overlap corresponds to (h\u00b7(J-I-h\u0303))_\u221e where J is the replication matrix\n\nConstraints:\n0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1, \u2211h = n/2\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\nPhase 1: Initialization\n   a. Set n_points=600 (should be 800 if sufficient budget) with dx=2/600\n   b. Interpolate high resolution parent solution using scikit-spline\n   c. Project solution to satisfy constraints:\n        h_proj = h_initial / (sum=h_initial * dx) * target_sum (adjusted by clipping)\n   d. Compute initial objective C0 = (np.max(np.correlate(h_proj, 1-h_proj))/n)*dx\n\nPhase 2: LogSE Optimization (Core Stage)\n   a. Optimize F(h,\u03b1) for \u03b1 in {10,5,3,2,1}:\n      i. Use L-BFGS-B with projected gradients\n      ii. Gradient computation: Backward pass through tensorized U\n      iii. Update h^{k}=h^{k-1} - \u03b3\u2207F(h^{k-1},\u03b1)\n   b. Line-search ensures global progress\n   c. Clip gradients when near boundaries\n   d. Maintain a reference solution for restarts\n\nPhase 3: Multi-Resolution Refinement (Avail.25% Time)\n   a. Interpolate key point to n=800 if time permits\n   b. Apply same optimization to finer grid\n   c. Compare against projected nearest neighbor in coarse grid\n\nPhase 4: Simulated Annealing (Final 5% Time)\n   a. Start from best solution found\n   b. Perturb h_new = h_best + \u0394(0.02*std_dev)\n   c. Accept with exp(-(F(h_new)-F(h_best))/T) if F increased\n   d. Cool T by factor of 0.99 each iteration\n   e. Final validation on original grid\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n   Variables:\n   - \u03b1 \u2208 {10,5,3,2,1}: Control LogSE smoothing\n   - n_stages=4: Polishing stages with increasing depth\n   - max_iter=100: per optimization phase\n   - Temperature schedule: 1000\u00d70.99 reduction\n   - \u0394_step=(0.5,0.1): multiplicative factor for perturbation\n\n   Key Configurations:\n   Config A (Basic):\n      n=600, \u03b1=3, 4 optimization stages, SA for 50% wall-time\n\n   Config B (Premium):\n      n=600 to 800 (4x resolution), \u03b1=10, 7 optimization stages, SA for 5% wall-time\n\n   Select based on budget:\n      Budget>300s \u2192 Config B\n      Budget\u2264300s \u2192 Config A\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n   CPU: 1 core\n   Timers:\n      - Monitor progress: 3 checkpoints/hundred iterations\n      - Analytics: Track convergence slope and objective gradients\n   Fallback Strategy:\n      a. If n=600 for>30s: Fall back to interpolated solution\n      b. If optimization stalls: Gradual gradient noise injection\n   Timeout:\n      Each optimization phase: 90% of total budget\n      SA phase: 10% of budget but capped at 300s\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n   Requirements:\n   1. np.all((h \u2265 0) & (h \u2264 1))\n   2. abs(sum(h)*dx - 1.0) < 1e-6\n   3. C_bound = -opt.hat_value + original_constant_factor  [implement properly]\n   4. Validate by recomputing max correlation on the grid\n\nImplementation Steps:\n1. Low-level components:\n   def correlate_tensor(h): returns full cross-correlation vector\n   def projected_gradient(h,\u03b1): returns 1/n* (formulated gradient aligned with [0,1])\n   def is_feasible(h): checks sum and bounds\n\n2. Hierarchical structure:\n   - Main solver\n   - Optimization manager (tracks budget/progress)\n   - Validation oracle (closed-form where possible)\n   - DAQ module (decision analytics queues for late detours)\n   \n3. Final return signature:\n   def run(seed=42,budget_s=1300):\n      h\",\"c5,n_points = self.solve()\n      return h,c5,n_points\n\nExecution Control:\n   Total budget calculation:\n   budget_used = solve_time + initial_interpolation_time + SA_time\n   Capacity slack: budget_s * 0.75",
